.TH FMT_TOHEX 3
.SH NAME
fmt_tohex \- convert a nibble to its hexadecimal character representation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <fmt.h>
.PP
.BI "char fmt_tohex(char " c ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fmt_tohex
converts the lower four bits (nibble) of the character
.I c
into its corresponding lowercase hexadecimal ASCII character ('0'-'9', 'a'-'f').
.PP
The function masks the input with 0x0F to isolate the lower nibble and returns the appropriate character constant from the internal hexadecimal digit table.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the hexadecimal character representing the value of the lower four bits of the input.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fmt_xlong (3),
.BR fmt_tohex_upper (3)